 "notes": "Blender Z up, faces -Y, character left = +X, metres; GLB export +Y up. Bone rolls 0. socket_offsets.loc are in the bone's local rest frame (metres from the bone head, Y along the bone; for the vertical head/neck bones local Z = world -Y = forward). Sockets head/neck/tail_tip are the SPEC 8 logical names; eyes is an extra (gaze beam origin, on the face between the eyes). Hierarchy: root -> pelvis; pelvis is the centre of gravity and parents BOTH spine_01 (up) and tail_01 (down the upright tail, round the bend at tail_03/04, then flat along +Y to the tip at tail_14). Rotating or moving pelvis moves the whole body incl. the grounded tail: LEAN RECIPE (bow, lean back, head to the floor): move the pelvis on an arc about the tail_03 head (0, -0.9145, 1.622), rotate the pelvis by the lean angle about the same axis, and counter-rotate tail_03 by minus that angle, so tail_03..14 stay on the ground (e.g. stunned = ~80 deg forward lean about X; see _lean in work/rig_review_medusa/stress.py). Decision (owner away): no re-parenting of the tail; animkit can wrap this as a helper. Tail is 14 even segments of 0.84 m (11.8 m from the pelvis to the tip; the tail lies 9.9 m along the ground behind the body, tip 9.3 m from the pelvis axis; SPEC 3.2/8 says ~14 m: kept the owner-sheet proportions, the lead should change SPEC to ~10 m; tail_swipe r 7 m is covered). Snake hair is fused into one mesh with the head (no separable snake islands), so there are 6 hair_* bones, one per visible snake (01 top, 03 bottom), each from inside the hair mass to the snake head. Weights (03b): neck+head and the shoulders are harmonic blends, so the back-hair curtain (fused to the upper back) grades spine_03 -> head from z 4.95 to ~5.95 and the shoulder tops carry no neck/head weight; the face above the jaw line is head 1.0; each snake ramps from head to its hair bone over the first 20 cm (55 cm for the low hair_*_03 snakes). Max edge stretch: head turn 45 / nod 40 ~5 cm, neck turn 35 ~4 cm, clavicle up 30 ~3 cm. FRAMING: split_sheet.png + cam.json (1920x1080) for idle, slither, gaze, stun_start, stunned, rise, hurt, death; split_sheet_tail_swipe.png + cam_tail_swipe.json (1920x1080, front +-10 m, side y -10.5..+10) for tail_swipe only."
